  "body": "Some time ago, for HTML5, the 'name' attribute for anchors was deprecated in preference for IDs where previously both were used.\r\n\r\nIf a dynamically generated website module (or any other content container) is used more than once on a page, then the use of IDs for the module is not a good idea as they would be duplicated. Not good practise. Therefore, the IDs can't be used and therefore there is no way to create an anchor to that content.\r\n\r\nThe use of the 'name' attribute - or any other attribute other than id - for anchors would be very useful when linking to dynamically generated content that can't have a unique ID added manually.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I propose that an attribute that doesn't need to be unique on a web page could be used instead of the ID where necessary.",
